2009/7/1 Tom Weissmann <tom.weissmann@gmail.com>:
> 2009/6/30 Pavel Machek <pavel@ucw.cz>:

> The PTS button is determined by 3 masks (button 1, 2, 3). I believe
> that if more than one mask is set, PTS will still only generate one
> click, not two simultaneous ones.

In fact it is possible set the masks to generate any combination of
button 1, 2, and 3 events (but not to distinguish events generated by
PTS from real button events).

With this in mind press-to-select could remain a boolean and the 3
button marks could be exposed as sysfs variables. Would this be
preferable?

Regards,
Tom
